rom_cache: drop RetroAchievements' client warning from achievementsets too

RetroAchievements answers achievementsets for a client it allows only casual
unlocks from -- RAOfflineProxy's User-Agent suffix is registered that way --
with a synthetic achievement prepended to the first set: CLIENT_WARNING_ID
101000001, "Warning: Casual Only" / "Hardcore unlocks cannot be earned using
this emulator.", MemAddr 1=1.300. so it pops five seconds in, 0 points
(RAWeb app/Connect/Actions/GetAchievementSetsAction.php and
CreateWarningAchievementAction.php). The server builds it with
Flags = FLAG_PROMOTED (3), the same flag as a core achievement.

The proxy already strips that id from patch, unlocks and startsession
responses (filter_warning_achievement_from_*), and rom_browser and storage
know the id too. The achievementsets filter, filter_warning_achievement_
definitions, keeps achievements by Flags == 3 alone -- so the server's
warning passes through it, online and from the cache, and an emulator on
the achievementsets API (RetroArch 1.22) sees every set one larger than the
site shows, awards 101000001 at every launch ("Achievement 101000001
awarded, new score: 0") with an unlock toast, and forwards that award to
RetroAchievements each time, since the server never records it as unlocked.

Drop the warning id in that filter as well, before the Flags test. Cached
achievementsets bodies are filtered on the way out (handle_offline_request
and the online path both go through filter_warning_achievements_for_action),
so a cache that already holds the warning serves sets without it from the
next launch; nothing else awards or re-awards the id once the emulator no
longer sees it. The Flags filter is unchanged.

Seen on ROCKNIX (fork issue maxengel/rocknix#166) with the proxy at
64d03d30633ca6e7719c26d732cef3c97dedcc27: three homebrew sets read 29/7/13
through the proxy against 28/6/12 direct, the extra being 101000001, awarded
five seconds into every proxied session. The Android filter
(ProxyServer.kt filterWarningAchievementDefinitions) has the same shape and
the same gap. Offered upstream as-is (ROCKNIX D-RA-002, D-RA-003: whatever
the fork changes in the proxy goes back).

--- a/linux/raofflineproxy/rom_cache.py
+++ b/linux/raofflineproxy/rom_cache.py
@@ -37,6 +37,12 @@ def filter_warning_achievement_ids(ids: list[int]) -> list[int]:
 
 
 def filter_warning_achievement_definitions(payload: dict) -> dict:
+    # RetroAchievements prepends its client warning (CLIENT_WARNING_ID,
+    # "Warning: Casual Only" for a client it allows casual unlocks from) to
+    # the first set with Flags=3, the same flag as a core achievement, so the
+    # Flags filter below keeps it. Drop it by id as the patch, unlocks and
+    # startsession filters do, or the emulator counts it in the set and
+    # awards it a few seconds into every session.
     filtered_payload = json.loads(json.dumps(payload))
 
     sets = filtered_payload.get("Sets")
@@ -53,6 +59,7 @@ def filter_warning_achievement_definitions(payload: dict) -> dict:
                 achievement
                 for achievement in achievements
                 if isinstance(achievement, dict)
+                and achievement.get("ID") != WARNING_ACHIEVEMENT_ID
                 and achievement.get("Flags", RC_ACHIEVEMENT_FLAG_CORE) == RC_ACHIEVEMENT_FLAG_CORE
             ]
 
